### 7f. BUG #3 — DB languages (mysql/postgresql/mongodb) bypassed the ECR pull
Symptom (ID 38/39/40): `db_runtime: create container: Error response from daemon:
No such image: code-runtime-mysql:latest` (NOT a pull/auth error).
Root cause: `internal/runtime/db_runtime.go` `runEphemeralDB()` calls the Docker SDK
`ContainerCreate` directly with the bare image name and never pulls — only the SANDBOX
path (`DockerSandbox.Execute` -> `ImagePool.EnsureImage`) does the registry-aware
pull+retag. So the bare `code-runtime-<db>:latest` was never fetched from ECR.
Fix: before ContainerCreate, ensure the image via the pool (pulls
`<registry>/code-runtime-<db>:latest`, retags to the bare name):
```go
if err := r.docker.ImagePool().EnsureImage(runCtx, spec.image); err != nil {
    return nil, fmt.Errorf("db_runtime: ensure image %q: %w", spec.image, err)
}
```
Rebuilt + pushed worker image as `coderuntime/worker:v2` and rolled out:
```bash
docker buildx build --platform linux/amd64 -f docker/Dockerfile.worker \
  -t 768054003064.dkr.ecr.ap-southeast-2.amazonaws.com/coderuntime/worker:v2 --push .
kubectl -n coderuntime set image deployment/worker \
  worker=768054003064.dkr.ecr.ap-southeast-2.amazonaws.com/coderuntime/worker:v2
```
RESULT: mysql(38)->Accepted "2", postgresql(39)->Accepted "2", mongodb(40)->Accepted "4".

