api-gateway was ClusterIP only; ingress had no controller. Exposed via a plain
`type: LoadBalancer` Service (in-tree AWS cloud provider -> Classic ELB; the AWS Load
Balancer Controller is NOT installed, so the `aws-load-balancer-type: external` annotation
must be omitted). Endpoint (HTTP:80, no TLS yet):
  http://aa6f9d7b568b4425f84ea155a296db33-71808099.ap-southeast-2.elb.amazonaws.com
  /health -> {"status":"ok","services":{"mysql":"ok","redis":"ok"}}

## Phase 8 — autoscaling validation + worker max 20 (KEDA -> cluster-autoscaler)
Goal: verify end-to-end autoscaling and raise the worker ceiling to 20 pods.

### 8a. KEDA worker max 1 -> 20
```bash
kubectl -n coderuntime patch scaledobject worker --type=merge -p '{"spec":{"maxReplicaCount":20}}'
```
Trigger = aws-sqs-queue, queueLength target=50 msgs/pod => desired = ceil(backlog/50), capped 20.
NOTE: with wait=true at client concurrency C, in-flight SQS msgs ~= C, so backlog stays < 50/pod
and workers DON'T scale. Drive scaling with an ingestion burst (--no-wait) that floods the queue.

### 8b. Node autoscaling (required for >~5 worker pods)
Each worker pod = worker(500m) + dind(250m) = 750m CPU; m7i-flex.large ~1930m allocatable
=> ~2 worker pods/node. 20 pods => ~10-11 nodes. So:
```bash
# raise managed nodegroup max 4 -> 12
aws eks update-nodegroup-config --cluster-name coderuntime --nodegroup-name system \
  --scaling-config minSize=2,maxSize=12,desiredSize=2 --region ap-southeast-2
# IAM policy + IRSA SA for cluster-autoscaler
aws iam create-policy --policy-name coderuntime-cluster-autoscaler --policy-document file://ca-policy.json
eksctl create iamserviceaccount --cluster=coderuntime --region ap-southeast-2 \
  --namespace=kube-system --name=cluster-autoscaler \
  --attach-policy-arn=arn:aws:iam::768054003064:policy/coderuntime-cluster-autoscaler \
  --override-existing-serviceaccounts --approve
# deploy cluster-autoscaler (autodiscovery via ASG tags k8s.io/cluster-autoscaler/{enabled,coderuntime})
kubectl apply -f eks/cluster-autoscaler.yaml   # image v1.32.0; RBAC incl volumeattachments + status cm Role
```
The eksctl managed nodegroup ASG is already tagged for autodiscovery.

### 8c. BUG #4 — dind startup race => new worker pods CrashLoopBackOff
Symptom on scale-up: `worker: fatal: sandbox: docker daemon unreachable: Cannot connect to the
Docker daemon at tcp://localhost:2375`. The worker fatals if the dind sidecar isn't accepting
connections yet; every new pod crash-loops until timing aligns (slows scale-up badly).
Fix: make dind a NATIVE SIDECAR — move it to initContainers with restartPolicy: Always and a
startupProbe (tcpSocket 2375). k8s then starts dind and waits for the probe BEFORE starting the
worker container. (worker connects via DOCKER_HOST=tcp://localhost:2375; dind listens
--host=tcp://0.0.0.0:2375.) After this, scale-up to 20 pods showed 0 crashes.

### 8d. RESULT — measured
- Ingestion burst: 1000 submissions -> 1000 accepted (100%), 166 req/s, p50 0.28s.
- KEDA: worker 1 -> 20 pods (backlog ~950 / 50).
- cluster-autoscaler: ASG 2 -> 11 nodes (max 12); pods Pending -> Running as nodes joined.
- Backlog 946 -> 0 with 16 workers running and 0 crashes (post native-sidecar fix).
- Scale-down: KEDA cooldown 120s -> worker back to 1; CA scale-down-unneeded 2m -> nodes back to 2.
